nfection was treated symptomatically, and his known Concussion / TBI was also reviewed.\n\nJune 09, Frazier was seen on June 9, 2021, for a follow-up regarding his Concussion / TBI. His blood pressure was 110/72 and weight 175 pounds. The patient reported doing well with no new symptoms, and his residual concussion symptoms were stable.\n\nSocial History:\nMr. Frazier reports consuming approximately six alcoholic drinks per He denies any current tobacco use.\n\nDr. Morse\nNeurology\nTrevino Harrison and Castro Clinic\n"
